Find references in docs/ that no longer resolve against this tree, and fix them.

A reference is anything the prose asserts exists in the code: a function or type name, a file
path, a CLI flag, an HTTP route, a make target, an environment variable. It "no longer resolves"
when the thing named is absent from the tree, or is named differently, or the doc describes a
signature or behaviour the code contradicts.

Only report what you have checked against the tree. A claim you could not verify is not a
finding — say so instead of guessing, and prefer a short list you are sure of over a long one
you are not. Do not rewrite prose you merely disagree with: this is about references that are
FALSE, not about style.

Read docs/working/contributing.md before you change anything, and hold to it: docs/ describes
what is true, docs/working/ and docs/roadmap/ are exempt because they describe what is coming.

Leave the tree building and the tests passing. Do not commit; edit the files and stop. Your
final message is the answer, so make it the list of what you changed and why each was wrong.
